---
/*  The host: the application that plays a DAW's tracks through the suite's plugins and its decoders. A
    product page, laid out as the plugins' pages will be: a picture of the window, what it does, its parts
    one band at a time, its numbers, and the way on to its tutorial. The bands are outlines until the
    pictures and the text exist. */
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import Cards from '../components/Cards.astro';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');

const bands = [
  { id: 'tracks', title: 'tracks', text: 'Which of the set’s tracks it hears, and where each one goes.' },
  { id: 'routing', title: 'routing', text: 'Sources into buses and returns, along wires, at one order.' },
  { id: 'decoders', title: 'decoders', text: 'Any number of them, each with a mix and outputs of its own.' },
  { id: 'timeline', title: 'timeline', text: 'The set’s transport, followed sample for sample.' },
];
---

<Page title="host" description="The application that plays a set's tracks through bambi.">
  <h1>host</h1>
  <p class="sub label">a whole set in ambisonics, played beside the DAW</p>

  <div class="prose">
    <p class="lede">
      The host plays the tracks of a set through bambi's plugins and decoders, routed as a field rather than as
      stereo, while the DAW keeps the arrangement and the transport.
    </p>
    <p class="fine">This page is being written. Its picture, its parts and its numbers come next.</p>
  </div>

  <section>
    <h2>where it runs</h2>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        The host works with Ableton Live. Other DAWs, and a way that works with any DAW on any system, are
        open: say on <a href="https://github.com/Looderso/bambi/issues">GitHub</a> which one you work in. What
        has been tried where is on <a href={`${base}/status`}>status</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  {
    bands.map((b) => (
      <section id={b.id}>
        <h2>{b.title}</h2>
        <p class="fine">{b.text}</p>
      </section>
    ))
  }

  <section>
    <h2>next</h2>
    <Cards
      items={[{ href: `${base}/tutorial/host`, title: 'the host', text: 'Setting up a set to play through bambi.', kind: 'tutorial' }]}
      style="row"
    />
  </section>
</Page>

<style>
  .sub {
    margin: 12px 0 var(--section);
  }
  section {
    margin-top: var(--section);
  }
</style>
